        "subHeading": "Compare AG Grid vs Handsontable on framework support, free and paid features, large datasets, pricing and licensing."
    },
    "shortAnswer": "AG Grid has a free, MIT-licensed Community edition that can be used commercially. Handsontable is a spreadsheet-style data grid whose free licence key covers non-commercial use, and evaluation and development, so commercial production use needs a paid licence. Both support React, Angular, Vue and JavaScript. AG Grid Enterprise includes pivoting, group-by-column row grouping and integrated charts; Handsontable's documentation does not list pivoting or built-in charts, and its nested rows show pre-structured parent and child rows.",
    "keyFigures": [
        {
            "value": "$0",
            "label": "AG Grid Community for commercial use",
            "detail": "MIT licence. Handsontable's free key is for non-commercial use."
        },
        {
            "value": "AI",
            "label": "Natural-language grid control",
            "detail": "Users query and change the grid in plain language with AG Grid's AI Toolkit."
        },
        {
            "value": "3",
            "label": "AG Grid features not in Handsontable",
            "detail": "Pivoting, integrated charts and the AI Toolkit."
        }
